; Tilo trusted-base SELinux confinement (CIL).
; ===========================================================================
; Confines the collaborative filesystem daemon (fs.service) into its own
; SELinux domain instead of the catch-all unconfined_service_t it lands in
; today (a custom binary with no policy = no MAC confinement). This is the
; MAC backstop for the trusted base: if fs is ever compromised, the kernel
; still boxes it.
;
; POSTURE: permissive-first.
; --------------------------
; The system runs SELinux ENFORCING and fs currently works. fs does a lot
; (FUSE mount of /var/workspace, iroh P2P networking, blob I/O under
; /var/cache, a unix control socket the compositor talks to), so the precise
; enforcing allow-set can only be finalised by capturing live AVCs on a real
; run. Shipping an incomplete ENFORCING domain would break a working daemon;
; shipping it PERMISSIVE logs every access without blocking, so fs keeps
; working AND we collect exactly the AVCs needed to tighten to enforcing.
; This is the standard SELinux bring-up workflow (permissive -> audit2allow ->
; enforcing), and is an honest improvement over unconfined_service_t.
;
; HOW fs ENTERS THE DOMAIN
; ------------------------
; fs.service carries `SELinuxContext=system_u:system_r:tilo_fs_t:s0` (drop-in),
; so systemd setexeccon's into tilo_fs_t at exec — no binary relabel needed
; (the executable stays bin_t; tilo_fs_t is allowed to entrypoint bin_t). The
; init_t -> tilo_fs_t transition is allowed explicitly (init_t is enforcing).

(type tilo_fs_t)
(typeattributeset domain (tilo_fs_t))
(roletype system_r tilo_fs_t)

; Permissive: log-but-allow everything tilo_fs_t does while the enforcing
; allow-set is being established from real AVCs.
(typepermissive tilo_fs_t)

; Let init (systemd) transition fs into the domain and entrypoint the binary
; (which keeps its default bin_t label — no relabel in the image).
(allow init_t tilo_fs_t (process (transition)))
(allow tilo_fs_t bin_t (file (entrypoint execute execute_no_trans read open getattr map ioctl)))
(allow init_t tilo_fs_t (process (siginh rlimitinh noatsecure)))

; The authenticated greetd session runs tilo-session in xdm_t. That wrapper
; starts and stops exactly one user lifecycle target before/after the native
; compositor. Give that target its own unit-file type so this does not grant
; xdm_t control over every systemd unit on the machine.
(type tilo_session_unit_file_t)
(roletype object_r tilo_session_unit_file_t)
(typeattributeset file_type (tilo_session_unit_file_t))
(typeattributeset non_auth_file_type (tilo_session_unit_file_t))
(typeattributeset systemd_unit_file_type (tilo_session_unit_file_t))
(filecon "/usr/lib/systemd/user/tilo-graphical-session.target" file
  (system_u object_r tilo_session_unit_file_t ((s0) (s0))))
(allow xdm_t tilo_session_unit_file_t (service (start stop status)))

; The compositor runs in that same xdm_t session and writes per-user state under
; $HOME through tilo-files' durable parent provisioning, which opens (O_RDONLY)
; and fsyncs every ancestor directory from / down. The base policy gives xdm_t
; getattr/open/search on /home (home_root_t) and read on everything below it,
; but not read on /home itself, and dontaudits that denial. So every such write
; from the session (e.g. the identity device fleet) failed with a bare EACCES.
; Only `read` on the /home directory is added; DAC (0755) already lets every
; local user list it, and nothing below /home is widened.
(allow xdm_t home_root_t (dir (read)))

; The console channel of a VM (crates/session/console-control): the greeter
; and the live installer run in xdm_t and answer the tilo-control action
; protocol on the virtio-serial port named org.tilo.console.0. That port only
; exists when a hypervisor attaches it (real hardware has no virtio-serial
; bus). 70-tilo-console.rules gives exactly that port to the greetd user;
; every other virtio port stays root-only by owner and mode, so this MAC
; grant does not widen who can open them.
(allow xdm_t virtio_device_t (chr_file (open read write getattr ioctl lock)))

; ENFORCING HARDENING PATH (do after a VM run captures AVCs):
; -----------------------------------------------------------
; 1. boot, exercise fs (mount /var/workspace, read/write, peer sync),
;    then: `ausearch -m AVC -ts boot | audit2allow -C` (or audit2allow -M).
; 2. translate the generated allow rules into CIL allows on tilo_fs_t here
;    (fuse, the iroh sockets, /var/workspace + /var/cache file types, the
;    control socket, capabilities), replacing `(typepermissive tilo_fs_t)`.
; 3. drop the permissive line so tilo_fs_t enforces.
; The compositor (shell) runs in the greetd session domain; giving it its own
; confined domain is the next base-daemon target, same workflow.
